# ABC Inventory Analysis

## Project Overview

ABC Analysis is an inventory classification technique used to
prioritize inventory based on its contribution to total inventory value.

## Objective

The objective of this project is to classify inventory into A, B,
and C categories and identify which products require the highest
level of inventory control.

## Dataset

The dataset contains:
- Product ID
- Annual Demand
- Unit Cost
- Annual Usage Value

## Methodology

1. Calculate Annual Usage Value
2. Sort products by Annual Usage Value
3. Calculate percentage of total value
4. Calculate cumulative percentage
5. Classify products into A, B, and C categories
6. Visualize the results
7. Provide inventory management recommendations

## Classification

A: 0–80% cumulative value
B: 80–95% cumulative value
C: 95–100% cumulative value

